# Artifact Repository Protocol

> A protocol: keep every meaningful conversation artifact as versioned GitHub content. One repo per project. Structured paths for code, docs, research, history, changelogs.

## Purpose
Explain the protocol as a filing rule, not as a running app. Source: fitzyracing1/artifact-repository-protocol.

## How it works (plain English)
1. One repo per project.
2. Put code, docs, research, history, and changelogs in named paths.
3. Version the artifacts.
4. Do not leave a useful file only in a chat.

## Key ideas
- One repo per project
- Versioned artifacts
- Structured paths

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/artifact-repository-protocol
repo = one_per_project()
paths = [code, docs, research, history, changelogs]
version(artifact)
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. one_per_project() → “do not dump all projects in one pile”
2. paths = ... → “named shelves inside the repo”
3. version(artifact) → “keep history of the file”

## Decisions the program makes
- If an artifact is only in chat → move it into the repo
- If two projects share a file → still keep one repo each

## What a person would notice
A filing law for conversation output.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the source and copy the path layout onto the next project.
